{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"YBVRAppleSDK"}],"roleHeading":"Protocol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ImmersiveOverlayRenderer","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ImmersiveOverlayRenderer","externalID":"s:12YBVRAppleSDK24ImmersiveOverlayRendererP","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ImmersiveOverlayRenderer"}],"symbolKind":"protocol"},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Inherits From","identifiers":["doc:\/\/applesdk.YBVRAppleSDK\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/applesdk.YBVRAppleSDK\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"inheritsFrom"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/applesdk.YBVRAppleSDK\/documentation\/YBVRAppleSDK\/ImmersiveOverlayRenderer","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ybvrapplesdk\/immersiveoverlayrenderer"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/applesdk.YBVRAppleSDK\/documentation\/YBVRAppleSDK"]]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Draws an app’s own content into the immersive video, in the same frame the SDK renders.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/applesdk.YBVRAppleSDK\/documentation\/YBVRAppleSDK\/ImmersiveOverlayRenderer\/draw(in:)"],"generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ImmersiveOverlayRenderer"},{"kind":"text","text":" : AnyObject, "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Sendable","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"}],"platforms":["visionOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Compositor Services surface owns the whole immersive space, so SwiftUI and RealityKit"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"content cannot be placed inside it. An overlay renderer is the way in: hand one to"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/applesdk.YBVRAppleSDK\/documentation\/YBVRAppleSDK\/VisionSurfaceContext\/init(layerRenderer:overlayRenderers:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and the SDK"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"calls ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/applesdk.YBVRAppleSDK\/documentation\/YBVRAppleSDK\/ImmersiveOverlayRenderer\/draw(in:)","isActive":true},{"text":" once per eye, every frame, after the video and the SDK’s own overlays","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"have been drawn - so whatever it draws lands on top of them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The SDK draws no subtitles of its own: it publishes ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/applesdk.YBVRAppleSDK\/documentation\/YBVRAppleSDK\/YBVRPlayerManager\/currentSubtitleCue","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"and leaves rendering it to the app. An overlay renderer is how an app puts that cue inside the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"immersive video; branding, or any HUD that should live in the video rather than in a window,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"goes the same way."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/applesdk.YBVRAppleSDK\/documentation\/YBVRAppleSDK\/ImmersiveOverlayRenderer\/draw(in:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" runs on the SDK’s render thread, not the main actor - hence"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Keep it short, and hand it whatever it draws through thread-safe state, such"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as an "},{"code":"OSAllocatedUnfairLock","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":".